                             v
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|                      EXECUTION PLANE                       |
|      (Kernel Telemetry, eBPF / PCAP Verification, I/O)     |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
```

2.1 The Reasoning Plane vs. Execution Plane

The Reasoning Plane hosts the agentic loop and operates in an unprivileged sandbox with zero direct access to system network sockets, database drivers, or persistent storage APIs. When an agent determines an action is required, it emits a structured tool-call intent rather than executing code directly.

The Execution Plane is a deterministic policy evaluation engine. It treats all inputs from the Reasoning Plane as untrusted byte streams.

2.2 Datapath Interception Mechanics

Interception occurs at the exact boundary where a tool call transitions from logical intent to system state change. Rather than relying on application-level middleware (which can be bypassed via object injection), datapath enforcement intercepts execution via a mandatory evaluation gate:

E(tau, sigma, pi) -> {ALLOW, DENY}

Where:

· tau represents the raw tool invocation payload.
· sigma represents the cryptographic source identity metadata.
· pi represents the deterministic policy rule set.

If evaluation fails or encounters an unhandled exception, the gate defaults strictly to DENY.

