6. Conclusion

Autonomous AI agents require infrastructure-grade security that matches their operational velocity. By combining Datapath Enforcement, Cryptographic Source Identity (Ed25519), Non-Compensatory Containment, and Kernel-Level eBPF Telemetry, this architecture reduces reliance on probabilistic LLM self-policing and declarative network policies.

The resulting framework provides a structured basis for audit transparency and a fail-closed posture. Formal verification, implementation validation, and independent peer review would be required before making publication-readiness claims for venues such as IEEE S&P or ACM CCS.

